  <iati-identifier>GB-COH-1762840-LEB141-HT10-01</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-COH-1762840" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HelpAge International</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Covid-19 Donation for Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HelpAge proposes to build on the existing activities and use the available structure and platforms to integrate the interventions focusing on Covid-19 and Cholera with the aim to reach out to the older Syrian and Lebanese populations in target areas. These proposed activities will be implemented following the recommendations from the relevant ministries such as the Ministry of Public health (MoPH), Ministry of Social Affairs (MOSA), Health, WASH and Protection clusters and other stakeholders actively working on the Cholera response. 

The major focus will be on prevention through information sharing on Cholera causes, symptoms, prevention and management, identification of suspected cases, guidance on health protocols to deal with Covid-19 and Cholera cases, information sharing on available services in the target areas and effective referrals, and through the provision of hygiene kits.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1:
Affected vulnerable families have improved access to Cholera preventive WASH services</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 2: 
Older people and people with disabilities and their family members feel safe and have increased capacity to cope with stressful situations</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will target vulnerable populations from Syrian refugees and host community members focusing on older women and men and persons with disabilities living in Beirut and Mount Lebanon governorates.</narrative>
  </description>
